{1 = 1-10}
9=1.	To make his name famous for all time until distant days, 
15=2.	and to transmit to posterity and the days  
19=3.	to come the praise poems of his power, 
23=4.	the songs of his might, 
27=5.	and the lasting fame of his exceptional intelligence, 
31=6.	King @wRN{Šulgi}, 
35=7.	king of @wSN{Urim}, 
39=8.	has brought the songs' latent wisdom before the mighty son of @wDN{Ninsumun}. 
43=9.	He praises his own power in song, 
47=10.	and lauds his own superior native intelligence: 

{11 = 11-20}
51=11.	I am a king, offspring begotten by a king and borne by a queen. 
55=12.	I, @wRN{Šulgi} the noble, 
59=13.	have been blessed with a favourable destiny right from the womb. 
63=14.	When I was small, I was at the academy, 
67=15.	where I learned the scribal art from the tablets of @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad}. 
71=16.	None of the nobles could write on clay as I could. 
75=17.	There where people regularly went for tutelage in the scribal art, 
80=18.	I qualified fully in subtraction, addition, reckoning and accounting. The fair @wDN{Nanibgal}, 
84=19.	@wDN{Nisaba}, provided me amply with knowledge and comprehension. 
88=20.	I am an experienced scribe who does not neglect a thing. 

{21 = 21-38}
92=21.	When I sprang up, 
96=22.	muscular as a cheetah, 
100=23.	galloping like a thoroughbred ass at full gallop, 
104=24.	the favour of @wDN{An} brought me joy; 
108=25.	to my delight @wDN{Enlil} spoke favourably about me, 
112=26.	and they gave me the sceptre because of my righteousness. 
116=27.	I place my foot on the neck of the foreign lands; 
120=28.	the fame of my weapons is established as far as the south, 
124=29.	and my victory is established in the highlands. 
128=30.	When I set off for battle and strife to a place that @wDN{Enlil} has commanded me, 
132=31.	I go ahead of the main body of my troops and I clear the terrain for my scouts. 
136=32.	I have a positive passion for weapons. 
140=33.	Not only do I carry lance and spear, 
144=34.	I also know how to handle slingstones with a sling. 
148=35.	The clay bullets, 
152=36.	the treacherous pellets that I shoot, 
156=37.	fly around like a violent rainstorm. 
160=38.	In my rage I do not let them miss. 

{39 = 39-51}
164=39.	I sow fear and confusion in the foreign land. 
168=40.	I look to my brother and friend, youthful @wDN{Utu}, 
172=41.	as a source of divine encouragement. I, @wRN{Šulgi}, converse with him whenever he rises over there; 
176=42.	he is the god who keeps a good eye on my battles. 
180=43.	The youth @wDN{Utu}, beloved in the mountains, 
184=44.	is the protective deity of my weapons; 
188=45.	by his words I am strengthened and made pugnacious (?). 
192=46.	In those battles, 
196=47.	where weapon clashes on weapon, @wDN{Utu} shines on me. 
200=48.	Thus I broke the weapons of the highlands over my knees, 
204=49.	and in the south placed a yoke on the neck of @wGN{Elam}. 
208=50.	I make the populations of the rebel lands -- how could they still resist my weapons? 
212=51.	-- scatter like seed-grain over @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad}. 

{52 = 52-55}
216=52.	Let me boast of what I have done. 
220=53.	The fame of my power is spread far and wide. 
224=54.	My wisdom is full of subtlety. 
228=55.	Do not my achievements surpass all qualifications? 

{56 = 56-76}
232=56.	I stride forward in majesty, trampling endlessly through the esparto grass and thickets, 
236=57.	capturing elephant after elephant, creatures of the plain; 
240=58.	and I put an end to the heroic roaring in the plains of the different liona, 
244=59.	the dragons of the plains, 
248=60.	wherever it approaches from and wherever it is going. 
252=61.	I do not go after them with a net, 
256=62.	nor do I lie in wait for them in a hide; 
260=63.	it comes to a confrontation of strength and weapons. 
264=64.	I do not hurl a weapon; 
268=65.	when I plunge a bitter-pointed lance in their throats, 
272=66.	I do not flinch at their roar. 
276=67.	I am not one to retreat to my hiding-place but, 
280=68.	as when one warrior kills another warrior, I do everything swiftly on the open plain. 
284=69.	In the desert where the paths peter out, 
288=70.	I reduce the roar at the lair to silence. 
292=71.	In the sheepfold and the cattle-pen, where heads are laid to rest (?), 
296=72.	I put the shepherd tribesmen at ease. 
300=73.	Let no one ever at any time say about me, 
304=74.	@q{“Could he really subdue them all on his own?”} 
308=75.	The number of lions that I have despatched with my weapons is limitless; 
312=76.	their total is unknown. 

{77 = 77-80}
