{175 = 175-189}
708=175.	I bestow joy and gladness, 
712=176.	and I pass my days in pomp and splendour. 
716=177.	But people should consider for themselves -- it is a matter  
720=178.	to keep in one's sights -- that at the inescapable end of life, 
724=179.	no one will be spared the bitter gall of the land of oppression. 
728=180.	But I am one who is powerful  
732=181.	enough to trust in his own power. 
736=182.	He who trusts in his own exalted name may carry out great things. 
740=183.	Why should he do less? 
744=184.	Since it was for my true mother @wDN{Ninsumun} that my mother  
748=185.	together with her actually bore me to bestow joy and gladness, 
752=186.	lovingly she cherished my unborn fruit. 
756=187.	She did not endure scandal from anyone's mouth. 
760=188.	Before she released her little one, 
764=189.	this lady passed her time in my palace in the greatest joy. 

{190 = 190-205}
768=190.	Before @wDN{Utu} son of @wDN{Ningal}, I, @wRN{Šulgi}, 
772=191.	declare that in my long life in which I have achieved great things since the day that my kingly destiny was determined, 
776=192.	in my life in which everything was richly provided in contentment, 
780=193.	I have never lacked anything. 
784=194.	Until the distant future may this song bless the name of me, 
788=195.	the king, with a life of long days. As I am musical, 
792=196.	as I am eloquent, I am a heavenly star of steadfastness. 
796=197.	It is an awe-inspiring brow that establishes palaces, 
800=198.	just as a peg and a measuring cord are the builders of cities. 
804=199.	With the awesomeness that radiates from my forehead, 
808=200.	which I make the foreign lands wear like a nose-rope, 
812=201.	and the fear-inspiring lustre, 
816=202.	my personal weapon, 
820=203.	which I impose on the Land like a neck-stock, 
824=204.	I am able to root out and undo crime. 
828=205.	I have the ability to reconcile great matters with one word. 

{206 = 206-220}
