1248=310.	May the scribe be on duty there and transcribe with his hand the prayers which I instituted in the @wTN{E-kur}; 
1252=311.	and may the singer perform, reciting from the text. 
1256=312.	The academies are never to be altered; 
1260=313.	the places of learning shall never cease to exist. 
1264=314.	This and this only is now my accumulated knowledge! 
1268=315.	The collected words of all the hymns that are in my honour supersede all other formulations. 
